1c257356ad864d0d606ddf5dfdf","position":"1787107240725663329-a8049c89-d454-4d44-822f-1fc7c602914b"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implemented the argparse refactor (behavior-preserving):\n\n- New shared `_seam.write_arg_parser()` -> `WriteArgParser(argparse.ArgumentParser)`: `add_help=False` (--help stays dispatcher-served byte-exact), `allow_abbrev=False` (exact-token, no prefix match), and an `error()` override that raises CommandError(returncode=1) — remapping argparse's 'expected one argument' to the historical 'Error: <flag> requires a value' (exit 1, not argparse's exit-2+usage). Callers use `parse_known_args` so unknown tokens are silently skipped.\n- transition._parse_flags RETAINED as a thin argparse-backed shim returning the identical 5-tuple (reason, force_reason, close_class, caused_by, ref). --reason/--class/--caused-by/--ref go through argparse; the retired --force-close is rejected up front by _reject_retired_force_close (argparse would silently skip it); the inline-only --force is handled explicitly by _extract_force (None=absent, ''=bare, '<r>'=reason; NEVER consumes a following token). Three external direct callers pass unchanged.\n- claim._parse_assignee now argparse-backed (None-vs-'' sentinel preserved: absent->None->default fallback, ''->cleared). claim._parse_force kept explicit (command-specific following-token rule, per the certified plan).\n- New tests/unit/test_claim_argparse_parse_fd48.py pins claim parser fidelity (None-vs-'', value-less exit-1 message, allow_abbrev, unknown-token skip, following-token --force).\n\nGates: make lint (ruff+format+complexity ratchet active=49 new=0 increased=0; _parse_flags complexity dropped below ceiling) + make typecheck green. Files under the 800 LOC cap (transition 707, claim 350, _seam 625). Pinning tests green: test_transition_force_flag_24f7, test_close_ref_target_80af, test_dependency_audit; 674 lifecycle/unit claim+transition tests pass.","timestamp":1787106660634965001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Pushed to Gerrit as change 1886 (https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1886), Change-Id Iff5432102c038105392d0312b616a989fa42b533, rebased onto origin/main 9f7407bb3d. Awaiting LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1.","timestamp":1787106754153344001}],"created_at":1787080925392033001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"0503c455-5e7c-4b2a-ac05-95e01a74a113","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"ba48-a88a-92bd-45d0"},{"link_uuid":"936415bf-4705-4b58-8a92-4a1eac88ead1","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"73b2-6194-c430-45ab"},{"link_uuid":"a8049c89-d454-4d44-822f-1fc7c602914b","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"0391-5ad1-251c-4b77"}],"description":"Standardize the CLI write-command argument parsing: retire the hand-rolled loop for Python's stdlib argparse, WITHOUT changing observable behavior. Behavior-preserving MECHANICAL adapter refactor.\n\n## Context / Problem\nThe CLI parses write-command args with a hand-rolled loop (claim.py `_parse_force`/`_parse_assignee`, transition.py `_parse_flags`) carrying bespoke semantics no schema reflects: `--assignee` ABSENT is a None sentinel (=> `ticket.default_assignee` fallback) while explicit `--assignee \"\"` CLEARS the assignee. Flags and `--help` can silently drift from behavior.\n\n## Dependency / sequencing\nDepends on blusterous-earthly-kitten, which normalized the force surface (removed `force_close`; made transition's `--force[=<reason>]` a reason-carrying param matching claim; dropped `--reason`-as-force-note). This refactor must preserve the POST-blusterous surface, so it runs AFTER that change to avoid re-encoding a soon-to-change flag and a conflicting edit on the same files.\n\n## Approach\nRefactor onto stdlib argparse (zero new runtime dep, portable, generates accurate `--help`); NOT Click/Typer. Respect the module-size (<=800 LOC) and per-function complexity ratchets by extracting along existing call-graph seams.\n\n### Behavioral fidelity (argparse defaults that MUST be overridden)\nThe hand loops have load-bearing behaviors argparse does not reproduce by default; preserve each:\n- **Unknown/extra tokens are silently skipped** — use `ArgumentParser(add_help=False)` + `parse_known_args()` (not `parse_args()`, which exits 2 on unrecognized args), discarding extras.\n- **`--help` is OUT OF SCOPE (parse-only refactor).** `-h`/`--help` is intercepted at the top-level dispatcher (src/rebar/_cli/__init__.py) and served BYTE-EXACT from the golden package help (src/rebar/_cli/help/claim.txt, transition.txt), pinned by tests (test_sub_help_equals_help_sub, test_schema_coverage.py); the command handlers never see `--help`. The argparse parser is NOT the help source, so `add_help=False` is safe and the goldens are untouched.\n- **Prefix-abbreviation disabled** — set `allow_abbrev=False` so `--for`/`--reas` do not match `--force`/`--reason` (the hand loops match exact spellings only).\n- **`--force` semantics DIFFER by command — preserve each exactly, do NOT unify:**\n  - claim `_parse_force`: `--force=<x>` -> x (empty -> \"(no reason given)\"); bare `--force` consumes the FOLLOWING token as the reason iff it does NOT start with `--`, else \"(no reason given)\". argparse's default handling differs on a following option-like token, so enforce the following-token/`--`-guard explicitly.\n  - transition `_parse_flags` (PARSER level): `--force=<x>` -> force_reason=x (incl. empty -> \"\"); bare `--force` -> force_reason=\"\" (NOT None) and MUST NOT consume the following token (test_force_does_not_swallow_a_following_token pins force_reason=\"\"). force_reason is None ONLY when `--force` is ABSENT. This three-state `str | None` (None=absent/not-forcing, \"\"=bare force, \"<r>\"=reason) is LOAD-BEARING: `_force_note()` maps None->\"\" (not forcing) and \"\"->\"(no reason given)\", and the None-vs-\"\" distinction drives the close-gate bypass. So the OBSERVABLE force note for a bare transition `--force` is \"(no reason given)\" — IDENTICAL to claim, matching the post-blusterous surface — even though the parser slot is \"\". Reason is supplied only via `--force=<reason>` (no following-token consumption).\n- **`--assignee` accepts `--assignee=<val>` AND space-separated `--assignee <val>` (next token consumed unconditionally); value-less at end exits 1** (\"Error: --assignee requires a value\"). Preserve None-vs-\"\" sentinel: ABSENT -> None; present (incl. \"\") -> that value.\n- **Retired `--force-close` keeps its exit-1 rejection** — transition rejects `--force-close`/`--force-close=<x>` with a bespoke message (test_transition_force_flag_24f7.py); argparse would silently skip it, so re-add an explicit pre/post-parse `CommandError(returncode=1)` with its message + rename guidance.\n- **Value-less/invalid-flag errors exit 1 with the current messages**, not argparse's default exit-2 + usage — use `exit_on_error=False` and/or catch `SystemExit`/`argparse.ArgumentError` and re-raise `CommandError(returncode=1)`.\n\n## Preserving direct callers of the private parse helpers\n`transition._parse_flags` is imported and called directly (unpacking its exact 5-tuple `(reason, force_reason, close_class, caused_by, ref)`, pinning None-vs-'' and the retired-flag rejection) by three tests OUTSIDE src/rebar/_commands/: tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_close_ref_target_80af.py, tests/unit/test_transition_force_flag_24f7.py, tests/scripts/test_dependency_audit.py. To keep them passing UNCHANGED, `_parse_flags` is RETAINED as a thin argparse-backed shim returning the identical 5-tuple/semantics. claim's `_parse_force`/`_parse_assignee` have no external direct callers (grep-verified) and may be replaced freely provided CLI-observable behavior is preserved.\n\n## Scope\n- src/rebar/_commands/claim.py — replace `_parse_force`/`_parse_assignee` with an argparse-backed parser, preserving the `--assignee` None-vs-\"\" sentinel.\n- src/rebar/_commands/transition.py — replace `_parse_flags`' hand loop with an argparse-backed parser, RETAINING `_parse_flags` as a shim returning the same 5-tuple.\n- Lib and MCP surfaces are OUT OF SCOPE (adapter-local change).\n\n## Testing\n- Existing CLI interface tests pass unchanged (tests/interfaces), incl. test_close_ref_target_80af.py's direct `_parse_flags` call (preserved via the shim).\n- Direct-caller unit/script tests pass unchanged: test_transition_force_flag_24f7.py (None-vs-'' + retired `--force-close` rejection), test_dependency_audit.py.\n- `--force[=<reason>]` inline + space-separated forms; bare -> \"(no reason given)\"; `--reason` only close_reason, never the force note.\n- `--assignee` absent => default_assignee fallback; \"\" => cleared; value-less => exit 1.\n- Unknown tokens silently skipped; retired `--force-close` exits 1; abbreviations do not match; ConcurrencyError exits 10.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] CLI write-command parsing goes through argparse (parse-only refactor); `--help` is UNCHANGED — still served byte-exact by the dispatcher from the golden help/claim.txt & help/transition.txt (test_sub_help_equals_help_sub + schema-coverage tests stay green), NOT regenerated from the parser.\n- [ ] The `--force[=<reason>]` reason-carrying form is preserved (bare -> \"(no reason given)\", `--force=<reason>` -> that reason); `--reason` is not repurposed as the force note (test).\n- [ ] The `--assignee` None-vs-empty-string distinction is preserved: absent => default_assignee fallback, \"\" => cleared (test asserts both).\n- [ ] `transition._parse_flags` is retained as an argparse-backed shim returning the identical 5-tuple, so its three external direct callers pass unchanged.\n- [ ] `--force` command-specific parser semantics preserved: claim bare `--force` -> next non-`--` token else \"(no reason given)\"; transition bare `--force` -> force_reason=\"\" (None only when absent) and does NOT swallow a following token — with `_force_note` the observable transition bare-force note is \"(no reason given)\", identical to claim. `--assignee` accepts inline `=value` AND a space-separated next token (consumed unconditionally), value-less => exit 1. `allow_abbrev=False` so partial spellings do not match (tests). `--assignee` accepts inline `=value` AND a space-separated next token (consumed unconditionally), value-less => exit 1. `allow_abbrev=False` so partial spellings do not match (tests).\n- [ ] argparse behavioral fidelity: unknown/extra tokens silently skipped (parse_known_args), retired `--force-close` keeps its exit-1 rejection, and value-less/invalid-flag errors exit 1 with existing messages (not argparse's exit-2 + usage).\n- [ ] Exit code 10 on ConcurrencyError is preserved (existing CLI interface tests pass).\n- [ ] `make lint` and `make typecheck` are green; module-size and complexity ratchets respected.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/claim.py","reason":"replace hand-rolled _parse_force/_parse_assignee loop with argparse"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/transition.py","reason":"standardize transition CLI arg parsing onto argparse"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["depends_on","73b2-6194-c430-45ab"],["relates_to","0391-5ad1-251c-4b77"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"8844376e-030d-4681-bb19-a0885156819e","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"fd48-7a80-33e9-4400","ticket_type":"story","title":"Standardize CLI write-command arg parsing (retire hand-rolled loop for a std framework)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["9871db77-246a-476c-90be-31da90295b16","936415bf-4705-4b58-8a92-4a1eac88ead1","62f48512-d273-421e-a960-8a2e4a6db700","c4260592-1f26-4fe9-93ca-73087bf9ba4e","04ab2692-8d17-4174-9ab4-508a34f7b3fa","00782a0b-cff0-4c83-9aad-b0b066a1c5ea","a6384142-3e78-454e-9585-d357cb74ab22","95777ae5-d8f6-4092-ad6c-73863b7f8936","7a6b6ec6-69a8-49c1-97cf-6942a6f04578","8844376e-030d-4681-bb19-a0885156819e","be1d460d-936d-4ee8-a0ab-1927926fcecf","1fb6dc09-5588-40f7-83f5-1d7d860b8150","b48908b3-9d02-4ed2-aeab-151a5d61a4fc","a8049c89-d454-4d44-822f-1fc7c602914b"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787107240725663330,"uuid":"6edf8ea9-f70b-4bd1-a502-d476c620bd9a"}